{"metadata":{"title":"LinkerSetsMacroSupport","externalID":"LinkerSetsMacroSupport","role":"collection","symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"LinkerSetsMacroSupport"}],"roleHeading":"Framework"},"abstract":[{"text":"The expansion behind every linker-set macro, for clients that declare a kind and a macro of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"their own.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro","doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetRecordMacro"],"title":"Declaring a macro","anchor":"Declaring-a-macro"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic"],"title":"Diagnostics","anchor":"Diagnostics"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/linkersetsmacrosupport"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@LinkerSetEntry(kind:)"},{"text":" takes its kind as an argument. A client that registers one kind of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"thing (routes, events, migrations) gives it a macro that fixes the kind instead, so its users","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"write ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Route"},{"text":" and never see a number. That takes three declarations.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The client’s compiler plugin, a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".macro"},{"type":"text","text":" target that depends on this module, names the kind:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import LinkerSetsMacroSupport","import SwiftCompilerPlugin","","@main","struct RoutesMacrosPlugin: CompilerPlugin {","    let providingMacros: [any Macro.Type] = [RouteMacro.self]","}","","public enum RouteMacro: LinkerSetMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> UInt32 { 0x726F_7574 }  \/\/ \"rout\"","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The client’s library declares the macro, the same kind, and the read of the set. It depends on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"LinkerSets and re-exports it, because the expansion calls LinkerSets’ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#linkerSetRecord"},{"type":"text","text":" in its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"users’ files:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["@_exported import LinkerSets","","extension LinkerSetKind {","    static let routes = LinkerSetKind(rawValue: 0x726F_7574)  \/\/ \"rout\"","}","","@attached(peer)","public macro Route() = #externalMacro(module: \"RoutesMacros\", type: \"RouteMacro\")","","extension Endpoints {","    public static var all: [Endpoint] {","        LinkerSet<Endpoint>(kind: .routes).values","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Its users then register routes and read them through the library:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["enum Endpoints {","    @Route static let home = Endpoint(path: \"\/\")","}","","let endpoints = Endpoints.all"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"text":"What the re-export exposes","level":3,"anchor":"What-the-re-export-exposes","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Route static let home = ..."},{"type":"text","text":" expands, in the user’s file, to one call:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#linkerSetRecord(kind: 0x726F7574, storing: Self.home)"},{"type":"text","text":". That macro, which LinkerSets declares,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"expands in turn to the record itself, one declaration per object format, naming"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSetsRuntime.LinkerSetRecord"},{"type":"text","text":". So the user’s file has to see LinkerSets. With"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@_exported import LinkerSets"},{"type":"text","text":" in the client’s library, importing the client is enough. With a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"plain or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"public import"},{"type":"text","text":", every user’s file fails to compile with “no macro named"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"‘linkerSetRecord’” until it imports LinkerSets itself. The compile tests in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tests\/CompileFailures"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ExportingClientUser"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ImportingClientUser"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ImportingClientUserImportingLinkerSets"},{"type":"text","text":") check each case."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"So every file that imports the client also sees ","type":"text"},{"code":"LinkerSet","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"LinkerSetKind","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and anything","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"public the client adds to them. A kind constant doesn’t need to be public: the macro writes the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"kind as a number, so users’ files never name the constant. Keep it internal and give users the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"values through the client’s own API, as ","type":"text"},{"code":"Endpoints.all","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" does above. A user can still read the set","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by its number, ","type":"text"},{"code":"LinkerSetKind(rawValue: 0x726F_7574)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; an internal constant only keeps it out of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"autocomplete and out of the client’s public API.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" writes the same record "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@LinkerSetEntry"},{"type":"text","text":" writes, in the same section, and its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"diagnostics name the client’s attribute ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"'@Route' applies to static members only"},{"type":"text","text":"). Each kind"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is a set of its own, so two clients in one program never see each other’s records as long as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"their kinds differ. Kind 0 is reserved, and the expansion refuses it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Registering types","level":3,"anchor":"Registering-types","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A macro attached to a struct, enum, class or actor stores the type’s metatype. To read the types","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as a protocol they share, without casting, the plugin names that protocol in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/requiredConformance(of:)","isActive":true},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["public enum EventMacro: LinkerSetMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> UInt32 { 0x6576_6E74 }  \/\/ \"evnt\"","","    public static func requiredConformance(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> TypeSyntax? {","        \"Events.AnalyticsEvent\"","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each record then holds "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"any AnalyticsEvent.Type"},{"type":"text","text":", read with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSet<any AnalyticsEvent.Type>(kind: .events).values"},{"type":"text","text":". A type that doesn’t conform fails to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"compile where it’s declared: “cannot convert value of type ‘NotAnEvent.Type’ to type"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"‘any AnalyticsEvent.Type’”. Qualify the protocol with its module so a type of the same name at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the use site can’t stand in for it. Without a required protocol, a type’s record holds"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Any.Type"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A registered type can be nested in another from swift-syntax 600 on. Before 600 a macro can’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"see where its declaration sits, so the type must be declared at file scope.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A macro that takes its kind as an argument can return "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/kindArgument(of:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/kind(of:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Declaring the kind once","level":3,"anchor":"Declaring-the-kind-once","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The plugin returns the kind from "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/kind(of:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and the library reads the set by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it, so the number appears twice, and a mismatch shows only at run time, as an empty set. To write"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it once, put it in a module of its own that depends on nothing, and have both import it:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["\/\/ RoutesKind","public enum RouteKind {","    public static let rawValue: UInt32 = 0x726F_7574  \/\/ \"rout\"","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"code":["\/\/ RoutesMacros, the plugin","public enum RouteMacro: LinkerSetMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> UInt32 { RouteKind.rawValue }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"code":["\/\/ Routes, the library","extension LinkerSetKind {","    static let routes = LinkerSetKind(rawValue: RouteKind.rawValue)","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The package lists the module among both targets’ dependencies:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".macro(name: \"RoutesMacros\", dependencies: [\"RoutesKind\", ...])"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".target(name: \"Routes\", dependencies: [\"RoutesKind\", \"RoutesMacros\", ...])"},{"type":"text","text":". SwiftPM builds it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for the host for the plugin and for the target for the library."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Writing records without depending on LinkerSets","level":3,"anchor":"Writing-records-without-depending-on-LinkerSets","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A module that uses ","type":"text"},{"code":"@LinkerSetEntry","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" depends on LinkerSets, which builds LinkerSets’ own plugin,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"LinkerSetsMacros, and swift-syntax with it. A module that only writes a few records, such as the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"events of one feature, can skip that. A client with a plugin of its own declares two macros there:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an entry macro that takes the kind as an argument, as ","type":"text"},{"code":"@LinkerSetEntry","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" does, and a record macro","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of its own under a different name, which the entry macro’s expansion calls in place of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"#linkerSetRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["\/\/ DiscoveryMacros, the plugin","@main","struct DiscoveryMacrosPlugin: CompilerPlugin {","    let providingMacros: [any Macro.Type] = [DiscoverableMacro.self, DiscoverableRecordMacro.self]","}","","public enum DiscoverableMacro: LinkerSetMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) throws -> UInt32 {","        try kindArgument(of: attribute)","    }","","    public static var recordMacroName: String { \"discoverableRecord\" }","}","","public enum DiscoverableRecordMacro: DeclarationMacro {","    public static func expansion(","        of node: some FreestandingMacroExpansionSyntax,","        in context: some MacroExpansionContext","    ) throws -> [DeclSyntax] {","        try LinkerSetRecordMacro.expansion(of: node, in: context)","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The library declares both and re-exports LinkerSetsRuntime, whose names the record uses:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["\/\/ Discovery, the library","@_exported import LinkerSetsRuntime","","@attached(peer)","public macro Discoverable(kind: UInt32) = #externalMacro(module: \"DiscoveryMacros\", type: \"DiscoverableMacro\")","","@freestanding(declaration)","public macro discoverableRecord<Value>(kind: UInt32, storing value: Value) = #externalMacro(module: \"DiscoveryMacros\", type: \"DiscoverableRecordMacro\")"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A module that writes records then depends on ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Discovery"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSetsRuntime"},{"text":", not on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"LinkerSets, and writes ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Discoverable(kind: 0x7365_7373)"},{"text":" where it would have written","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@LinkerSetEntry(kind: 0x7365_7373)"},{"text":". Its build holds the client’s plugin, which already","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"needs swift-syntax, and not LinkerSetsMacros. The record macro’s name must differ from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"linkerSetRecord"},{"text":", because a module that imports both LinkerSets and the client couldn’t choose","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"between two macros of the same name.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Testing the expansion","level":3,"anchor":"Testing-the-expansion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A client’s expansion tests pin one line per record, the ","type":"text"},{"code":"#linkerSetRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" call:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["assertMacroExpansion(","    \"\"\"","    enum Endpoints {","        @Route","        static let home = Endpoint(path: \"\/\")","    }","    \"\"\",","    expandedSource: \"\"\"","    enum Endpoints {","        static let home = Endpoint(path: \"\/\")","","        #linkerSetRecord(kind: 0x726F7574, storing: Self.home)","    }","    \"\"\",","    macroSpecs: [\"Route\": MacroSpec(type: RouteMacro.self)],","    failureHandler: { Issue.record(\"\\($0.message)\") }",")"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"assertMacroExpansion"},{"type":"text","text":" expands only the macros in its table, so the call stays as written, and it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reads the same on every swift-syntax from 600 on. The record behind it, one declaration per object"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"format, belongs to LinkerSets and changes when LinkerSets adds a format. A test that wants it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"anyway adds "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"linkerSetRecord\": MacroSpec(type: LinkerSetRecordMacro.self)"},{"type":"text","text":" to the table. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"declaration at file scope expands to the call inside a private enum of its own, whose name comes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the context’s unique names ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"__macro_local_15linkerSetRecordfMu_"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Writing the expansion yourself","level":3,"anchor":"Writing-the-expansion-yourself","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" supplies the peer "},{"code":"expansion","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A macro that needs more writes its own and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"calls "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/recordPeers(of:providingPeersOf:in:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" from it for the record. That’s how"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a macro adds the conformance as well, so its users write "},{"code":"@Event struct Login {}","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" without naming"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the protocol. The macro takes an extension role beside the peer:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["public enum EventMacro: LinkerSetMacro, ExtensionMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> UInt32 { 0x6576_6E74 }  \/\/ \"evnt\"","","    public static func requiredConformance(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> TypeSyntax? {","        \"Events.AnalyticsEvent\"","    }","","    \/\/ The record, as a peer.","    public static func expansion(","        of node: AttributeSyntax,","        providingPeersOf declaration: some DeclSyntaxProtocol,","        in context: some MacroExpansionContext","    ) throws -> [DeclSyntax] {","        try recordPeers(of: node, providingPeersOf: declaration, in: context)","    }","","    \/\/ The conformance the record requires, as an extension.","    public static func expansion(","        of node: AttributeSyntax,","        attachedTo declaration: some DeclGroupSyntax,","        providingExtensionsOf type: some TypeSyntaxProtocol,","        conformingTo protocols: [TypeSyntax],","        in context: some MacroExpansionContext","    ) throws -> [ExtensionDeclSyntax] {","        [try ExtensionDeclSyntax(\"extension \\(type.trimmed): Events.AnalyticsEvent {}\")]","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The library declares the macro with both roles:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["@attached(peer)","@attached(extension, conformances: AnalyticsEvent)","public macro Event() = #externalMacro(module: \"EventsMacros\", type: \"EventMacro\")"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A type can then carry data of its own through the protocol (a schema, a name) while the record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"holds only its metatype, read as ","type":"text"},{"code":"LinkerSet<any AnalyticsEvent.Type>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Skipping a record instead of refusing it","level":3,"anchor":"Skipping-a-record-instead-of-refusing-it","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The expansion refuses what a record can’t hold with an error. A macro that would rather skip some","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of those (a generic event that its library lists by hand, say) asks","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/refusal(of:providingPeersOf:in:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" first. It returns a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" whose ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic\/reason-swift.property","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" says why, and whose","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic\/node","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is where to report it, or ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when the declaration can hold a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["public static func expansion(","    of node: AttributeSyntax,","    providingPeersOf declaration: some DeclSyntaxProtocol,","    in context: some MacroExpansionContext",") throws -> [DeclSyntax] {","    if let refusal = try refusal(of: node, providingPeersOf: declaration, in: context),","       refusal.reason == .genericType {","        context.diagnose(Diagnostic(node: refusal.node, message: GenericEventNote()))","        return []","    }","    return try recordPeers(of: node, providingPeersOf: declaration, in: context)","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every other refusal still reaches "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/recordPeers(of:providingPeersOf:in:)"},{"type":"text","text":", which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"throws it. Where a declaration sits (in a function’s body, a protocol or a generic type) is seen"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from swift-syntax 600 on; before it those three aren’t returned, and the compiler refuses them in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the expansion."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://LinkerSetsMacroSupport/documentation/LinkerSetsMacroSupport/LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic":{"url":"\/documentation\/linkersetsmacrosupport\/linkersetmacrodiagnostic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Why a linker-set macro refuses a declaration or a kind, with the message the compiler shows,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"naming the macro as it was written (","type":"text"},{"code":"@Route","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), and the node the message points at.","type":"text"}],"title":"LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic"}]},"doc://LinkerSetsMacroSupport/documentation/LinkerSetsMacroSupport/LinkerSetRecordMacro":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"code":"#linkerSetRecord(kind:storing:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": one record of ","type":"text"},{"code":"kind","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" whose accessor stores the expression,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"written in the section LinkerSets owns, under ","type":"text"},{"code":"#if objectFormat(...)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with one declaration per","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"object 